cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  news-aggregator: span-level reporting of language techniques in Polish news headlines
message: >-
  If you cite the measurements in this repository, cite the release they were taken from.
  The figures describe one configuration — model, prompt version and input variant — and
  MODEL_CARD.md records which.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bińkowski
    given-names: Dawid
    email: d.k.binkowski@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/binkowskidawid/news-aggregator
abstract: >-
  Fetches Polish news articles, classifies them by topic, and reports specific language
  techniques in the headline and lead, each anchored to the verbatim quote it is about. Every
  model call runs on hardware the operator controls. Measured on 64 held-out articles: the
  underline lands on a fragment an annotator also marked in 47% of cases, the technique named
  beside it is also correct in 42%, and 100% of quotes were found verbatim in the source. A
  quote that cannot be located in the source text is discarded rather than repaired.
keywords:
  - persuasion technique detection
  - Polish
  - media analysis
  - large language models
  - span extraction
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
